{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRD3UgAedYSsJaNxXZsM6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"118\t\n119\t## Consequences\n120\t\n121\tADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\n122\tis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\n123\tentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n124\t\n125\tADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\n126\tcreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n127\t`client: true` or the keep list.\n128\t\n129\tAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\n130\tlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\n131\tnot the attribute.\n132\t\n133\tA bound prop is read-only inside the component. Calling the setup prop\n134\tsignal with a value while a signal or computed is bound throws an error\n135\tnaming the tag and the prop, so a component cannot write page state\n136\tdirectly and a write to a computed is not silently dropped. Unbound\n137\tprops stay writable by their own component.\n138\t\n139\tThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\n140\tcondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n141\t`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n142\t\n143\tThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\n144\thydration example uses it.\n145\t\n146\t## Notes\n147\t\n148\t2026-10-14: component children originally shared the region marker.\n149\tA kept component whose render had a reactive region before its\n150\tchildren was then adopted against the wrong range, leaving the\n151\tchildren's listeners unbound. Children now open with `<!--[c-->`.\n152\tServer output changes only for components with non-empty children;\n153\tstatic pages are byte-identical.\n154\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f36234a9-39f9-42b6-adfe-69bb0c6f7c55","uuid":"9e5bf576-6353-4ada-8037-0ab57c5eb9fa","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:13:27.199Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-04-raw-adoption-alignment/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","content":"\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nA bound prop is read-only inside the component. Calling the setup prop\nsignal with a value while a signal or computed is bound throws an error\nnaming the tag and the prop, so a component cannot write page state\ndirectly and a write to a computed is not silently dropped. Unbound\nprops stay writable by their own component.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.\n\n## Notes\n\n2026-10-14: component children originally shared the region marker.\nA kept component whose render had a reactive region before its\nchildren was then adopted against the wrong range, leaving the\nchildren's listeners unbound. Children now open with `<!--[c-->`.\nServer output changes only for components with non-empty children;\nstatic pages are byte-identical.\n","numLines":37,"startLine":118,"totalLines":154}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FRD3UgAedYSsJaNxXZsM6Y","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
